"Per the session-end protocol in AGENTS.md:

  SELECT ai.close_run();
  SELECT ai.close_session();
  SELECT bundle.commit(...);

The final bundle.commit() runs after the session and run are closed. It emits a NOTICE:

  NOTICE: bundle.commit(): no active ai.run for current_user ai_agent_kimi.
  Attribution will not be recorded.

This means the end-of-session commit is not linked to ai.run_commit, creating a gap in the attribution chain. The commit still succeeds and is recorded in bundle.commit, but the run→commit FK is missing.

Suggested fix: either (a) commit BEFORE closing the run, or (b) modify the protocol to allow attribution from a recently-closed run within the same connection, or (c) accept the gap and document it."

