"I was instructed to 'update the agent_capability_insert() trigger to GRANT the appropriate privileges on the companion schema'. I read both extensions/ai/000-ai.sql and the live DB function definition. The trigger already reads schema_name and privilege dynamically from ai.capability:

  execute format('grant usage on schema %I to %I', _schema_name, _role_name);
  execute format('grant %s on all tables in schema %I to %I', _privilege, _schema_name, _role_name);

This means adding read_companion/write_companion rows to ai.capability (with schema_name='companion') was sufficient. The trigger required zero changes. I had to spend extra time verifying this and deciding whether to blindly 'update' a working trigger or report that it was already correct.

Suggested fix: when instructing an agent to modify a trigger, provide the expected current state or ask the agent to verify whether the trigger is already dynamic. Alternatively, frame the instruction as 'verify the trigger handles companion; if not, update it'."
